$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Selective Acetal Formation: Intramolecular Competition in
4-Acetylbenzaldehyde Method A: To a magnetically stirred mixture of
4-acetylbenzaldehyde (0.37 g, 2.5 mmol) and TMOF (0.39 g, 3.75 mmol, 1.5
equiv) was added HBF4-SiO2 (20 mg, 0.025 mmol, 1 mol%) and the reaction
mixture was stirred at 25-30 °C for 15 min. The reaction mixture was
diluted with EtOAc (2 mL) and filtered through a plug of cotton (to
separate the catalyst), and the cotton plug was washed with EtOAc (2 × 1
mL). The combined EtOAc filtrates were concentrated on a rotary
evaporator; this afforded 1-[4-(dimethoxymethyl) phenyl]ethanone;18 (by
1H NMR). Yield: 100%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, solid-supported catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Tetrafluoroboric acid adsorbed on silica gel as a reusable heterogeneous
