$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of Acetals. General Procedure. To a magnetically stirred
mixture of the corresponding aldehyde (1 equiv, 5 mmol) and trimethyl
orthoformate (1.2 equiv, 6 mmol) in methanol (1 M) was added p-TsOH·H2O
(0.01 equiv, 1 mol %), and the mixture was stirred at room temperature
until completion of the reaction (12-24 h, TLC). The mixture was
extracted with H2O/Et2O. The combined Et2O extracts were dried (Na2SO4)
and concentrated under reduced pressure, and the product was obtained as
a colorless oil and used without purification.
(3,3-Dimethoxypropyl)benzene (1b). Compound 1b was prepared according to
the general procedure and was obtained in >99% yield (0.9013 g, 5 mmol)
as a colorless oil. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.28-7.02 (m, 5H), 4.30 (t,
J = 5.7 Hz, 1H), 3.26 (s, 6H), 2.60 (dd, J = 9.0, 7.0 Hz, 2H), 1.85 (ddd,
J = 10.0, 8.0, 5.9 Hz, 2H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 141.8, 128.5,
126.0, 103.9, 52.9, 34.2, 31.0.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
