$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure A To a solution of the corresponding
carbonyl compound 4 (3 mmol) in ethanol (2 mL) or triethyl orthoformate
(2 mL) or ethanol/triethyl orthoformate mixtures in a molar ratio of 4:3
the corresponding catalyst (20 or 40 mg) was added and the reaction
mixture was stirred, at 353 K, for the reaction time shown in Tables 1
and 2. The isolation of the product was carried out as follows: (i)
filtration of the catalyst and (ii) the excess of ethanol or triethyl
orthoformate were removed in vacuo. 1,1-Diethoxy-heptane (3a). Table 2
Acetalation/ketalation reaction catalyzed by Al-SBA-15 in the presence of
triethyl orthoformate or/and ethanol Diethoxymethyl-benzene (3b). Yield
100%. νmax/cm-1 1260, 1092, 1053, 1016, 799; δH (400 MHz; CDCl3) 1.25 (6
H, t J1,3 7.2 Hz, 2 CH3), 3.67-3.52 (4 H, 2 m, 2 CH2), 7.39-7.30 (3 H, m,
aromatics), 7.49 (2 H, d J1,3 8 Hz, aromatics); δC (100 MHz; CDCl3) 15.1,
60.9, 101.4, 126.5, 128.0, 128.1, 139.0.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, alternative reaction conditions gave lower yield,
alternative preparation shown, Zeolite Al-SBA-15 used as catalyst
