$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of Diethyl Acetals; General Procedure: To a mixture of
carbonyl compound 1 (5 mmol) and (EtO)3CH(10-12.5 mmol), WCl6 (0.05-0.1
mmol) was added, and the resulting solution was stirred at room
temperature and the progress of the reaction was monitored by TLC or GC
After completion of the reaction (Table 1), a cooled aqueous solution or
NaOH (10%,25 mL) was added and the mixture was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 x
25 mL). The organic extracts was washed with water (2 x25 mL) and dried
over anhydrous Na2SO4. Evaporation of the solvent under reduced pressure
gave almost pure product(s). Further purification was proceeded by vacuum
distillation to afford pure diethyl acetal 2 in good to excellent yield
(Table 1). 2a, yield 98%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
