$DATUM 5470-11-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 67-56-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure B: Catalytic acetalization. To a
mixture of the carbonyl compound (1.5 mmol) in MeOH (HPLC grade, 5 mL),
hydroxylamine hydrochloride (0.15 mmol) and powdered sodium hydroxide
(0.15 mmol) were added in that order. The reaction was stirred for 18 h,
then 3 mL of saturated NH4Cl and 3 mL of H2O were added. The mixture was
extracted with diethyl ether (3 x 10 mL); the combined organic layers
were washed with brine (10 mL), dried (MgSO4), and concentrated by rotary
evaporation. Catalytic procedure: Cyclohexane carboxaldehyde (0.20 mL,
1.7 mmol) was dissolved in MeOH (5.0 mL) and reacted with hydroxylamine
hydrochloride (0.012 g, 0.18 mmol) and powdered sodium hydroxide (0.006
g, 0.15 mmol) according to procedure B above. Benzene acetaldehyde
dimethyl acetal 1k. Benzene acetaldehyde (0.20 mL, 1.7 mmol) was
dissolved in MeOH (5.7 mL) and reacted with hydroxylamine hydrochloride
(0.012 g, 0.171 mmol) and powdered sodium hydroxide (0.007 g, 0.17 mmol)
according to procedure B above. The acetal (0.283 g, 99%) was isolated as
a clear, colorless oil. 1H NMR and 13C NMR spectra correlated with those
reported in the literature.[9]
