$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Methylene Acetal
Forming Reaction Promoted by PhSCH2OCH3, DBDMH, and BHT (Table 2). DBDMH
(1.5 equiv) was added to a solution of diol 1 (1.0 equiv), BHT (1.5
equiv), and methoxymethyl phenyl sulfide (1.5 equiv) in CH3CN (0.2 M) at
room temperature under N2. After 1 was consumed (monitored by TLC), 10%
aqueous KOH (2 mL) was added to the reaction mixture ,and the mixture was
extracted with Et2O (30 mL × 3). The combined organic layers were dried
over Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was
subjected to flash column chromatography (SiO2). Entry 1: According to
the general procedure, the treatment of diol 1d (101.1 mg, 0.500 mmol)
with DBDMH (214.4 mg, 0.750 mmol), BHT (165.3 mg, 0.750 mmol) and
methoxymethyl phenyl sulfide (110.0 μL, 0.750 mmol) for 20 min. Eluent,
hexanes → hexanes/Et2O (50/1). 4-Decyl-1,3-dioxolane, 2d, (105.0 mg,
98%). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.85 (t, J = 6.7 Hz, 3H), 1.15-1.65 (m,
18H), 3.36-3.42 (m, 1H), 3.90-3.99 (m, 2H), 4.84 (s, 1H), 4.99 (s, 1H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM reaction monitored by TLC
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Methylene Acetal Formation from 1,2- and 1,3-Diols Using an O,S-Acetal,
1,3-Dibromo-5,5-dimethylhydantoin, and BHT
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
