$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3-(Dimethoxymethyl)-1-phenyl-2,3-dihydro-1H-naphtho[1,2-e][1,3]oxazine
(10) To a stirred solution of Betti base 8 (2.49 g, 10 mmol) in MeOH (30
mL) was added an aqueous solution of 2,2-dimethoxyacetaldehyde (60 wt%,
1.81 g, 12 mmol) at r.t. The resulting mixture was stirred continuously
for another 1 h, the white solid 10 formed was collected by filtration,
and purified by chromatography (silica gel, PE-EtOAc, 5:1). Usually, it
was directly used in the next step without purification. Yield (3.28 g,
98%). mp 147-149 °C (CH2Cl2-MeOH). IR (KBr): 2900, 1620, 1440, 1210, 1230
cm-1. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ = 7.70-7.64 (m, 2 H), 7.28-7.13 (m, 9 H), 5.43
(s, 1 H), 4.74-4.71 (m, 1 H), 4.42-4.41 (m, 1 H), 3.39 (s, 6 H),
2.86-2.83 (m, 1 H). 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ = 151.6, 142.1, 131.2, 129.0 (2
C), 128.8, 128.5, 128.2, 128.0 (2 C), 127.0, 126.3, 123.0, 122.5, 119.0,
114.3, 103.4, 81.3, 55.6, 55.2, 52.7. MS (EI): m/z (%) = 432 (M+, 0.01),
231 (100). Anal. Calcd for C21H21NO3: C, 75.20; H, 6.31; N, 4.18. Found:
C, 75.13; H, 6.41; N, 4.12.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM a modest rate acceleration observed with 10% water
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM An efficient method for the preparation of versatile building blocks:
1-substituted 2,2-dimethoxsyethylamine hydrochlorides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
