$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the preparation of 1,3-dioxanes via in-situ
transacetalization; To a solution of carbonyl compound 1 (5 mmol),
1,3-propanediol (7.5-10 mmol), and (EtO)3CH (5 mmol) in dry CH2Cl2 (15
mL), ZrCl4 (0.05-0.15 mmol) was added and the resulting solution was
stirred at room temperature. After completion of the reaction (TLC or
GC), the reaction was quenched with a cold aqueous solution of NaOH (10%,
25 mL) and the organic layer was separated and the residue was extracted
with CH2Cl2 (3 × 40 mL). The organic extracts were combined together and
washed with water (3 × 35 mL), and dried over anhydrous Na2SO4.
Evaporation of the solvent under reduced pressure gave almost pure
1,3-dioxane 3. Further purification was achieved by vacuum distillation
or recrystallization from the appropriate solvent to give pure product(s)
in good to excellent yields (Table 1). Product 3a, yield 98%.
