$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure A: Synthesis of acetals
1a-i. To a solution of aldehyde 2a-c (3.0 mmol) in toluene (10 mL) were
added molecular sieves (5Å, 4 g), benzylic alcohol 3a-e (38.6 mmol, 12.7
eq.) and pyridinium p-toluenesulfonate (20 mg, 0.08 mmol, 0.03 eq.). The
suspension was stirred at room temperature until no further conversion
could be observed as judged by 1H NMR spectroscopic analysis. After
diluting with EtOAc (100 mL) and filtrating through a pad of Celite®, the
reaction mixture was washed with sat. aq. NaHCO3-solution (30 mL), washed
with brine (30 mL) and dried over MgSO4. The solvents were removed under
reduced pressure and the crude product was subjected to column
chromatography using a double-walled, water cooled column (petroleum
ether-EtOAc). According to general procedure A 2-butenal (2a) (0.3 mL,
3.6 mmol) was reacted with benzyl alcohol (3a) (4.7 mL, 45.3 mmol, 12.7
eq.). The reaction was worked up after 19 h and acetal 1a was isolated
after column chromatography (petroleum ether-EtOAc, 95:5).
3-Methyl-2-butenal-bisbenzyl acetal (1d). According to general procedure
A 3-methyl-2-butenal (2b) (0.3 mL, 3.0 mmol) was reacted with benzyl
alcohol (3a) (4.0 mL, 38.6 mmol, 12.7 eq.). The reaction was worked up
after 2 d and acetal 1d was isolated after column chromatography
(petroleum ether-EtOAc, 95:05) as colourless oil (830 mg, 97%). Rf = 0.5
(petroleum ether-EtOAc, 90:10). FT-IR (film): 3031, 2912, 2869, 1679,
1497, 1454, 1377, 1202, 1138, 1072, 1035, 1020, 932, 693, 732 cm-1. 1H
NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 1.69 (d, 4J = 1.0 Hz, 3 H, 4-Ha), 1.77 (d, 4J =
1.1 Hz, 3 H, 3-CH3), 4.57 (d, 2J = 11.7, 2 H, 1'-Ha), 4.66 (d, 2J = 11.7,
2 H, 1'-Hb), 5.37 (d, 3J = 6.6, 1 H, 1-H), 5.43-5.44 (m, 1 H, 2-H),
7.27-7.34 (m, 10 H, 3'-H, 4'-H, 5'-H) ppm. 13C NMR (151 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
18.6 (C-4), 25.7 (C-3-CH3), 66.9 (C-1'), 98.0 (C-1), 122.4 (C-2), 127.5
(C-4'), 127.9 and 128.4 (C-3' and C-4'), 138.4 and 138.8 (C-3 and C-2')
ppm. MS (EI, 70 eV): m/z (%) = 175 (50, [(M-OBn)+]), 91 (100, C7H7+),
HRMS (FT-ICR-MS): m/z calcd. for C19H23O2 + Na: 305.1517; found:
305.1513.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM scalable, molecular sieves used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A mild PPTS-catalyzed acetalization of α,β-unsaturated aldehydes: the
first single-step protocol towards benzylic acetals
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Boese, Dietrich; Luebcke, Marvin; Pietruszka, Joerg
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2013), 45(6), 729-733

